## Layer Contract

- **Plugins** declare routes and contain handlers inline. Each handler validates input (via the validator), calls exactly one repository method, and returns a response. No Prisma calls in plugins.
- **Repositories** own all Prisma calls. They do not validate input or check ownership.
- **Validators** expose typed `validate<Entity>Create` / `validate<Entity>Update` functions backed by Zod schemas.
- **auth.plugin.ts** registers `@fastify/jwt` and decorates `fastify.authenticate` — a preHandler applied to all write routes when auth is enabled.

## Security Invariants

These are enforced by the generated code and must not be removed:

1. **Integer ID validation** — `parseId` in every plugin rejects floats, alpha strings, SQL-injection suffixes, and overflow values. Never bypass it.
{% if auth_entity_name %}2. **Owner FK injection** — the `{{ auth_entity_name | lower }}Id` FK is always set from `request.user.id` inside the plugin. It is never read from the request body. The Zod validator excludes it from all schemas.
3. **Ownership check before mutation** — `PUT` and `DELETE` handlers fetch the existing record and compare its owner FK against `request.user.id` before proceeding. Do not remove these checks.
4. **Auth entity self-ownership** — users may only update/delete their own `{{ auth_entity_name }}` record; the plugin enforces `request.user.id === id`.
5. **Sensitive fields hashed** — fields marked `@llm sensitive` in the schema are hashed with bcrypt before storage and excluded from all API responses and the JWT payload.
6. **JWT required on writes** — `fastify.authenticate` preHandler is applied to all `POST`, `PUT`, and `DELETE` routes. Reads may be public depending on the schema.
{% else %}2. **Ownership check before mutation** — if an entity has an owner FK, `PUT` and `DELETE` handlers fetch the existing record and compare its owner FK against `request.user.id` before proceeding.
{% endif %}
## Adding a Feature

Follow the layer contract strictly:

1. Add routes and handlers in `src/plugins/<entity>.plugin.ts` — validate input with `validate<Entity>Create/Update`, inject owner FK from `request.user.id`, call the repository
2. Add the data-access method in `src/repositories/<entity>.repository.ts`
3. If new fields are needed, update `src/validators/<entity>.validator.ts` (Zod schemas) and `src/types/<entity>.types.ts`

Never put Prisma calls in a plugin handler. Never put validation logic in a repository.

## Error Handling

Throw typed errors from `src/lib/errors.ts`; the global `setErrorHandler` in `src/app.ts` maps them to HTTP status codes:

| Class | Status |
|---|---|
| `ValidationError` | 400 |
| `AppError(401, ...)` | 401 |
| `AppError(403, ...)` | 403 |
| `NotFoundError` | 404 |
| `ConflictError` | 409 |

Any unhandled error returns 500. Do not send raw error messages to the client.

